{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And further</b> [ויותר]. עוד means 'to persist,' as in עוד טומאתו בו (his impurity is still in him)." "<b>And listened</b> [ואזן]. [Either] poems or compositions, from the balances [אזני] of wisdom; or it is from ears [אזנים], like the matter of hearing." "<b>And searched out</b> [וחקר]. It is ways for the people to investigate wisdom in them, and it will be a transitive verb [פועל יוצא] taking two objects [שנים פעולים]." "<b>He set in order many proverbs</b> [תקן משלים הרבה]. And he spoke three thousand proverbs."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:20.722309169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}